      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Statutory RTO Paperwork, Transit Marine Insurance &amp; Delivery Handover for Bike Transportation Ghosi Insured</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">
	<p>When transporting your bike to Ghosi, it is crucial to have the following documents and certificates in order to ensure a smooth and hassle-free process.</p>

	<p>The Registration Certificate (RC) is a vital document that proves ownership of the bike. To facilitate the transportation process, a self-attested photocopy of the RC is required. This photocopy must be provided to the transportation company or transporter before they can proceed with the transportation.</p>

	<p>To ensure the bike is in a roadworthy condition, a valid Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate is necessary. The PUC verifies that the bike meets environmental standards and is fit to be driven on the roads. Make sure to provide a valid and current PUC to the transporter.</p>

	<p>To protect both you and the transporter, it is essential to provide a valid insurance certificate for the bike. This certificate ensures that in case of any accident or damage during transportation, the financial responsibility is covered. Ensure that the insurance is up-to-date and valid for the entire transportation process.</p>

	<p>To ensure transparency and accountability during the transportation process, it is recommended to obtain an IBA-approved (Indian Bicycle Association) consignment bill of lading. This document serves as a legally binding agreement between you and the transporter, detailing the terms and conditions of the transportation.</p>

	<p>To provide extra protection for your bike during transportation, 100% declared-value marine transit insurance is essential. This insurance policy covers your bike against any damage or loss during the transportation process, ensuring your peace of mind. Make sure to declare the true value of your bike to the insurance company for accurate coverage.</p>
	<h3>Important Note:</h3>
	<p>Before signing any agreement or documents with the transporter, make sure to thoroughly read and understand the terms and conditions. Additionally, it is advisable to keep a copy of all the mentioned documents for your records.</p>
