      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Ghosi</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>The handover of a two‑wheeler or motorcycle at its final destination is a critical step that ensures the vehicle’s condition, mileage, and delivery terms are formally verified. This process is performed during daylight to allow clear visual comparison with the original pickup documentation and to provide optimal lighting for detailed inspections.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>
    <p><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection Against Pickup Photos</strong></p>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The delivery team compares the current state of the vehicle with the photographs taken at pickup. Visual checkpoints include body panels, paint finish, scratches, dents, tire tread, and any existing damage.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Any discrepancies noted during the daylight re‑inspection are documented with new photographs, annotated with timestamps and reference to the original pickup images.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>If significant damage is identified, the consignee and the carrier’s representative sign a variance report before proceeding to the next verification stage.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>

  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>
    <p><strong>Odometer Verification Against the LR Bilty</strong></p>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The driver records the final odometer reading on the LR (Lorry Receipt) bilty, which already contains the initial mileage at dispatch.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>A physical inspection of the odometer is performed to confirm it is mechanical or electronic and not tampered with.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The difference between the final and initial readings is calculated and entered into the handover form, ensuring the mileage aligns with the consignment’s contractual terms.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>

  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>
    <p><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong></p>
    <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Both the consignor’s authorized representative and the carrier’s driver review the completed inspection reports, odometer verification, and any variance notes.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>Once all parties are satisfied, a formal condition sign‑off sheet is executed, detailing the vehicle’s final condition, mileage, and any observed wear‑and‑tear.</span></li>
      <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The signed document serves as legal proof that the handover was completed under daylight conditions, with all verification steps properly recorded, thereby closing the delivery transaction.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </span></li>
</ul>

<p>This structured daylight handover protocol safeguards both the carrier and consignee by providing a transparent, documented, and mutually agreed‑upon conclusion to the two‑wheeler or motorcycle delivery process.</p></div>
